1
00:00:00,216 --> 00:00:02,232
A customer calls Concrete again.

2
00:00:02,771 --> 00:00:07,395
What should the next customer service agent know before asking the first question?

3
00:00:07,913 --> 00:00:09,282
Not just a phone number.

4
00:00:09,479 --> 00:00:11,433
but the correct customer profile

5
00:00:11,572 --> 00:00:12,911
the available history,

6
00:00:13,231 --> 00:00:15,552
and the notes attached to previous calls.

7
00:00:16,171 --> 00:00:19,801
Here's the second experience GRINDCTRL is proposing for Concrete.

8
00:00:20,301 --> 00:00:21,963
A clearer customer view.

9
00:00:22,242 --> 00:00:26,595
connected to incoming calls through Genesys and the appropriate Zoho records.

10
00:00:27,073 --> 00:00:29,068
The caller number initiates a lookup.

11
00:00:29,590 --> 00:00:30,948
After a reliable match,

12
00:00:31,248 --> 00:00:34,905
The agent sees the customer's name and permitted contact details.

13
00:00:35,182 --> 00:00:36,912
including email when available.

14
00:00:37,309 --> 00:00:39,740
Missing information is marked unavailable.

15
00:00:40,116 --> 00:00:45,447
The same proposed view can show the customer segment from Concrete Icons Club. Lifestyle.

16
00:00:45,485 --> 00:00:46,877
Prestige or Elite.

17
00:00:47,335 --> 00:00:51,552
That membership information must come from a trusted, updated source.

18
00:00:52,032 --> 00:00:54,194
It cannot be guessed from the caller's number.

19
00:00:54,473 --> 00:00:58,032
and no membership benefit should be assumed without confirmation.

20
00:00:58,391 --> 00:01:00,853
But a profile is only the starting point.

21
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:03,265
Call-level history matters more.

22
00:01:03,722 --> 00:01:09,308
Imagine a simple timeline showing every available call activity. its date, agent

23
00:01:09,511 --> 00:01:13,067
and notes for that specific interaction. For example,

24
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:15,974
Last week's call concerned an exchange request.

25
00:01:16,394 --> 00:01:19,256
The employee recorded that the branch would review the matter.

26
00:01:19,555 --> 00:01:21,416
When the customer calls again today,

27
00:01:21,655 --> 00:01:25,781
The new agent opens that particular call and reads its actual note.

28
00:01:26,140 --> 00:01:27,894
They see what was documented.

29
00:01:28,112 --> 00:01:31,932
Without confusing a call note with a ticket comment... AI summary,

30
00:01:32,173 --> 00:01:33,455
or a completed action.

31
00:01:33,797 --> 00:01:35,392
During today's conversation,

32
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:39,631
The agent records a new note against the right interaction if supported.

33
00:01:40,030 --> 00:01:42,411
Notes should belong to the call they describe.

34
00:01:42,730 --> 00:01:44,081
not a generic summary.

35
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,817
And the interface must handle uncertainty honestly.

36
00:01:48,217 --> 00:01:49,351
No matching contact?

37
00:01:49,774 --> 00:01:50,952
offer a manual search.

38
00:01:51,456 --> 00:01:52,491
Multiple matches?

39
00:01:52,913 --> 00:01:55,176
Ask the agent to select the right record.

40
00:01:55,556 --> 00:01:56,829
Missing membership data?

41
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:58,327
Mark it unavailable.

42
00:01:58,650 --> 00:02:00,130
Lookup temporarily down?

43
00:02:00,470 --> 00:02:02,183
Never block the incoming call.

44
00:02:02,541 --> 00:02:07,557
Before implementation, we'll verify where call activities and notes actually live.

45
00:02:07,894 --> 00:02:09,567
which integrations are supported,

46
00:02:09,765 --> 00:02:11,762
and who is allowed to see each field.

47
00:02:12,221 --> 00:02:15,581
Then we'll test with authorized fictional customer records.

48
00:02:15,981 --> 00:02:18,564
The outcome we're aiming for is continuity.

49
00:02:18,923 --> 00:02:23,204
a more informed employee, and a customer who doesn't have to start from zero.

50
00:02:23,483 --> 00:02:24,858
every single time.
